# 05 LSP & Code Intelligence *05-lsp*

## 1. What is LSP *lsp-intro*

The Language Server Protocol (LSP) powers all code
intelligence in this configuration. It provides:
autocompletion, live diagnostics (errors/warnings),
go-to-definition, project-wide rename, formatting,
and hover type information. Each language you work
with has a dedicated LSP server (rust-analyzer,
pyright, ts_ls, lua_ls, etc.).

## 2. Installing LSP Servers *install-lsp*

Open `:Mason`, search for the language server you
need, and press `i` to install. For example, search
`pyright` to add Python support.

After installation, open a file in that language
and run `:LspInfo` to verify the server is attached.
If you see "No client attached", check that Mason
has the server installed.

## 3. Autocompletion (blink.cmp) *autocompletion*

The completion menu appears automatically as you
type. Key controls:

- `<Tab>` — Select next item
- `<S-Tab>` — Select previous item
- `<CR>` — Confirm selection
- Auto — Documentation preview pane

Snippet expansion and signature help work out of
the box — function parameter hints appear when you
type `(`.

## 4. Diagnostics (Trouble) *diagnostics*

- `<leader>xx` — Open full diagnostic list
- `<leader>xX` — Buffer-level diagnostics only

Press Enter to jump to the error location. Press `q`
to close. Diagnostics are grouped by severity —
Errors and Warnings are clearly separated.

## 5. Navigation & Jumping *navigation*

- `<C-]>` — Go to definition
- `K` — Hover to show type signature and docs
- `:IcUseage` — Show incoming calls for the symbol

Press `Ctrl+o` to jump back after navigating.

## 6. Code Actions *code-actions*

Press `<C-x>a` to open the LSP Actions menu. This
gives you quick fixes (auto-import missing modules),
code generation (getters/setters), and refactoring
operations. Select an action and press Enter to
apply it.

## 7. Formatting & Renaming *format-rename*

- `:IcFormat` — Format the current file
- `:IcRename` — Rename symbol project-wide

Renaming is cross-file — all references update
automatically.

## 8. Symbol Search *symbol-search*

- `<leader>cs` — Document/workspace symbol search
  (Trouble)
- `<F3>` — Toggle Outline symbol tree

Use `<leader>cs` in large files to quickly locate
classes, functions, and definitions.

## 9. LSP Restart *lsp-restart*

If an LSP server hangs or you've changed its
configuration, run `:IcLspRestart` to restart the
server for the current buffer. No need to restart
Neovim.

## 10. Advanced Trouble Usage *trouble-advanced*

- `<leader>cl` — View LSP references/definitions
- `:Trouble qflist toggle` — Toggle quickfix list
- `r` — Rename symbol from Trouble

Trouble is more than a diagnostic viewer — it's the
unified panel for all LSP results.

## 11. Summary *summary*

You now have the full LSP workflow: install servers
→ autocomplete → check diagnostics → navigate code
→ apply code actions → format and rename. This covers
90% of code intelligence needs in daily development.
